<title>USA: Ground broken for Raleigh, N.C., arena.</title>
<headline>Ground broken for Raleigh, N.C., arena.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's Centennial Authority broke ground Monday on a $132 million arena in Raleigh to house the North Carolina State University basketball team and the Carolina Hurricanes National Hockey League team.</p>
<p>The authority plans to issue about $57 million of tax-exempt revenue projects for the arena by year-end. The 21,000-seat facility is scheduled to open in 1999.</p>
<p>The arena is being financed with $22 million of state revenues, $70 million of Raleigh and Wake County hotel taxes, plus private funds raised by NCSU boosters.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
